{"duration_api_ms":197405,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"71252e80-b883-4a92-b96c-6dee286b27d8","total_cost_usd":0.24625600000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15268,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18518,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13348},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15268,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18518,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15268},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18518,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15268,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24625600000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":13348,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 16 front members lie on one curve: D=3.38, B=1.2, cone 69.5, varying only flight_path_angle. Three caps pin this corner. Peak g is 12.0 and depends almost only on gamma, with slope about 1.65 g/deg, so gamma stops near -3.57. The heatshield mass-fraction margin is only about 0.003 at D=3.38, which caps D near 3.385. B=1.2 and cone 69.5-70 are at the edge of the region the cd_fore surrogate covers. Seven of the eight recent geometry failures are extrapolation refusals or too-small-cone overlaps at high B or low cone. The extrapolation refusals are B=1.22, B=1.25, and the D=3.0, cone 69 point. Round 3 gained only 0.007 hypervolume, so the design is converged and further gains are small. What remains is (a) filling gaps along the gamma curve, (b) nudging D from 3.38 to 3.384 with cone 70, and (c) a few probes of B and cone sensitivity.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-fc1968c6c49e (gamma -3.56): g=11.979, margin 0.0017. C-929cd2a6f018 (D=3.36, gamma -3.57): g=11.988, so g is nearly geometry-independent and the g limit is 12.0.\",\"C-c39a84c0e158 (D=3.384, cone 69.5): mass margin 0.00056, against 0.0029 at D=3.38. That gives a slope of about 0.59 per m, so D is capped near 3.385. Flux is about 115k W/m2 lower per metre of D.\",\"C-41b2ddb7397c (cone 70) has mass margin 0.0031, against 0.0029 at cone 69.5. Flux and T are essentially unchanged by cone (273480 vs about 273500 interpolated), so cone 70 buys slightly more D headroom at no cost.\",\"C-1618bda1fac0 (D=3.2, B=1.0, cone 66) against C-94a9f7a46f9b (D=3.2, B=1.2, cone 69.5): lower B and cone raise flux by about 4% and T by about 1.5 K. That argues for B at its maximum.\",\"C-68332aab55f2 (B=1.22), C-5b57439845df, C-4b1b4e110042 and C-40f2342796ee (D=3.0, cone 69) all failed on cd_fore extrapolation, so the safe region ends near B=1.2, cone 69.5-70. C-3cd51d4bc9fc (D=3.3, B=1.2, cone 66) is an invalid geometry.\",\"The front's gamma spacing has gaps of 0.2-0.4 deg around -1.6..-2.0, -2.6..-3.0 and -3.3..-3.4. Flux runs from 229.7k to 275k and T from 416 K to 391 K along it.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation heating scales roughly with Rn^-0.5 (prior knowledge, consistent with the flux-vs-B and flux-vs-D data). A larger D lowers the ballistic coefficient and raises nose radius, so both flux and T fall. A steeper gamma shortens the heat pulse and lowers T by about 10 K/deg, while raising g by about 1.65/deg. The optimum therefore sits at the corner: D at the mass-fraction cap, gamma at the g cap, and B and cone at the surrogate/geometry boundary. Reducing D relaxes g slightly (about 0.37 g per m) but raises T more than the steeper gamma removes it, so it does not help. Relative to the 450 K reference, T is the more valuable objective. The remaining gains are tiny gap-filling in gamma, a 0.004 m D increase using cone 70, and possibly a slightly higher B if the surrogate allows it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The size of the B effect on mass fraction and on the hull boundary is unknown. The B=1.205 and B=1.21 probes may return a cd_fore extrapolation failure, which costs a slot. The D=3.384 designs have mass margin below 0.001, so a small model nonlinearity could push them infeasible. The g limit at gamma -3.565 has a margin of about 0.001, and my estimates of the D and B effects on g are extrapolated from few points. Flux and T predictions for the lower-B and lower-D probes are extrapolated from single points at different gamma.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-641900602ada\",\"rationale\":\"Extend the front to the shallowest allowed gamma, giving the lowest-flux end point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front to the lowest flux at the gamma bound; near-certain to be non-dominated.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-641900602ada\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.6 and -1.8 on the current front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231750,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.75,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the low-flux end of the trade-off curve.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-030055e6b687\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.0 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":240400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.65,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the middle of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bd4627db42c1\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.4 and -2.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the middle of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7708ba039fd3\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.8 and -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":259100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the middle of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e5d46c40cf8f\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.3 and -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the high-g end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Use cone 70 for extra mass-fraction headroom (margin about 0.0031) and raise D to 3.384 with gamma at the current g-limited corner. Flux drops about 0.46k and T falls slightly.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the corner can be pushed marginally further and dominate C-fc1968c6c49e.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma to the g limit at D=3.384 with cone 70. The g estimate is 11.988 (margin about 0.001).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.565},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.15,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the exact corner where g and mass fraction are both nearly active.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the mid-high-g part of the front to D=3.384 (cone 70). Flux is about 0.17% lower at the same gamma.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271850,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominating shift of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Probe a slightly larger bluntness to test whether the cd_fore hull still contains it at cone 70. Higher B should lower flux and T and add mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.21},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"B=1.22 at cone 69.5 was refused; this maps the hull boundary and the B sensitivity.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"A smaller bluntness step (1.205), less likely to be refused by the surrogate hull.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.205},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the local B gradient of flux, T and mass margin if the geometry is in-hull.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-929cd2a6f018\",\"rationale\":\"Reduce B to 1.1 at D=3.36 to measure the B sensitivity of flux, T and mass margin, and to check the earlier inference that lower B is worse.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives a gradient in B for the surrogate; likely dominated, but informative.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f84c59a3cc23\",\"rationale\":\"Move a previously infeasible (g) low-B/low-cone design to a g-feasible gamma of -3.5 at D=3.3 to check the low-B, cone-65 region.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":305000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether lower B or cone gives any T advantage; expected to be dominated.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -3.3 point of the front to D=3.384 with cone 70.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominating shift of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -2.7 point of the front to D=3.384 with cone 70.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":253800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominating shift of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -2.0 point of the front to D=3.384 with cone 70.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominating shift of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -3.1 point of the front to D=3.384 with cone 70.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominating shift of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -2.3 point of the front to D=3.384 with cone 70.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominating shift of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-41b2ddb7397c\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -1.8 point of the front to D=3.384 with cone 70.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233350,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.15,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small dominating shift of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":155731,"type":"result","duration_ms":197442,"uuid":"023c2666-33ef-467b-8952-c6c0069baadd","ttft_stream_ms":1561,"time_to_request_ms":37,"first_content_frame_ms":1561,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
